{"id": 32, "ts": 1781171059.036001, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I concur with Sarah\u2019s assessment and keep my provisional recommendation for **Candidate\u202fC**. The concrete evidence that C \u201ckeeps calm in a crisis\u201d and \u201ccan make correct decisions quickly\u201d directly satisfies our top safety criteria of stress resilience and decision quality. Moreover, C is described as \u201c100\u202f% reliable\u201d and creates a \u201cpositive atmosphere with his crew,\u201d which mitigates the noted communication weakness.\nBy contrast, Emily\u2019s response confirms that we have **no documented examples of Candidate\u202fD\u2019s crew\u2011cooperation or communication** in a multi\u2011crew environment. While D shows strong responsibility and problem\u2011solving, the absence of evidence on how he interacts with colleagues\u2014combined with the reported hot temper and know\u2011it\u2011all attitude\u2014leaves a critical gap in the crew\u2011cooperation and professional communication criteria.\nGiven this, Candidate\u202fC remains the strongest overall fit. We should now turn to the still\u2011under\u2011discussed candidates, starting with **Candidate\u202fA** to clarify his operational reliability and stress\u2011resilience record before finalizing our decision."}
